          <msContents>
            <summary>Livre premier de la Théorique de la vertié de l'alchemie plus utille qu'on ne sçauroit estimer pour acquérir la congnoissance d'icelle. [Followed by] Livre second de la praticque. The second part contains chemical receipts and remedies. At the end of the text, on fol. 35v of the second part, is an entry: '1767 aoust 8 M. Vialette Chirurgien a purger [sic] le père De St. Flour et lui a donné le 9, 10, 11 du quina en bols et Mr. Corundet [Cormidet?] a purger [sic] et fourni des médicaments à Mr. Boyer'. Below this 'Du 4 juin 1773 Mr. Lubres [?]'.</summary>
            <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">French</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_432_1">
              <author/>
              <title type="original">Livre priemier de la Theorique</title>
              <title type="standard"/>
              <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">French</textLang>
              <filiation>This MS. may possibly be a French version of the 'Testamentum' by-or attributed to-Raymundus Lullius. It is divided into a 'Théorique' and a 'Pratique', but the text does not seem to correspond either with the Latin, or with the French MSS. recorded in Mrs. Singer's Bibliography Nos. 244 et seq.</filiation>
            </msItem>
          </msContents>
